<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro de la Gasca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1493">1493</a>–1567</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro de la Gasca was a Spanish priest and royal official sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> in 1546 to end the rebellion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-pizarro">Gonzalo Pizarro</a>. Offering pardons and the repeal of the harshest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-laws">New Laws</a>, he won over most rebels, defeated Pizarro at Jaquijahuana in 1548 and had him executed, then reorganised the colony before returning to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, where he became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palencia">Palencia</a> and later of Sigüenza.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pedro-de-la-gasca.jpg" alt="Pedro de la Gasca" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Valentin Carderera y Solano · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pedro_de_la_Gasca.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
